{
  "about": "One table of cases for the rules of a duel and a tour, played by the device's domain tour/ (Vitest) and by the backend's AroundTheWorld.Domain.Tours (xUnit), so the two implementations stay equal (docs/adr/0033-deciding-a-game-on-the-server.md). A duel's answers are given in order, each by the traveller, the desk holder or another player, with the time in milliseconds from the card appearing; a tour's duels are decided in order, each won by one side at a time in milliseconds of game time. T is the first traveller; Pn is seated at desk n.",
  "duels": [
    {
